adr: 0210
file: selfhost/apfront.pas
kills: pascalc-product
why: the defect this fixed, put back. curFile is the client's by the time Sema runs -- the import loop restores it before returning -- so a diagnostic about an imported component's block carried the client's name and the component's line number, which is a position the named file need not have. Every case under tests/ stays green with the defect in: run_test.sh translates each component separately and first and gives up if one fails, so no case can reach a component that does not translate on its own being handed to --import anyway. Only the probe in producttest sees it.
--- old
  if m^.mdFileIdx > 0 then curFile := importName[m^.mdFileIdx];
--- new
  if false then curFile := importName[m^.mdFileIdx];
